*> Test US12-client (docs/protocol/40-menus-4 section 4.9; 002-lane-stations T5201): the stonecutter's list is the entries of the latest Update Recipes (0x88): the result item
*> and count of each, a malformed packet changes nothing; the screen of menu type 24 has a clickable entry and an item stack for each entry from SC-START (12 at most), the
*> selected entry (data slot 0) highlighted; an empty list has none; the wheel moves the first visible entry by a row within the offscreen rows and does nothing for a list of 12.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-STONECUTTER-SCREEN.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-SERVER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 4096.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEFT                BINARY-LONG VALUE 100.
 01 WS-TOP                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 50.
 01 WS-DIR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PACKET              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-BAD                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 99.
 01 WS-N1                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N2                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N3                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-E1                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E2                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E3                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E4                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E5                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(200).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SERVER
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     PERFORM PACKET-3
     CALL "STONECUTTER-READ" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-4§4.9 Update Recipes with three stonecutter entries keeps their result items and counts" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SC-COUNT TO WS-E1
     MOVE SC-ITEM(1) TO WS-E2
     MOVE SC-ITEM(3) TO WS-E3
     MOVE SC-AMOUNT(2) TO WS-E4
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "3 10 12 2" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-4§4.9 a truncated packet changes nothing" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 5 TO SC-START
     MOVE 40 TO PB-LENGTH
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     MOVE 3 TO PB-LENGTH
     CALL "STONECUTTER-READ" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER
     MOVE SC-COUNT TO WS-E1
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-E2
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "3 5" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-4§4.9 type 24 shows an entry and a stack per list entry, the selected one highlighted (state 1)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 24 TO BM-TYPE
     MOVE 1 TO BM-DATA(1)
     MOVE 0 TO SC-START
     MOVE 0 TO SM-WIDGET-COUNT
     CALL "STONECUTTER-DECOR" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-LEFT WS-TOP
     MOVE SM-WIDGET-COUNT TO WS-E1
     MOVE SM-W-KIND(1) TO WS-E2
     MOVE SM-W-ARG(2) TO WS-E3
     MOVE SM-W-STATE(3) TO WS-E4
     MOVE SM-W-X(5) TO WS-E5
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E5)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "6 4 801 1 184" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-4§4.9 an empty list has no widgets" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO SC-COUNT SM-WIDGET-COUNT
     CALL "STONECUTTER-DECOR" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-LEFT WS-TOP
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SM-WIDGET-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-4§4.9 a list of 20 entries moves by a row with the wheel and stops at the last offscreen row (2); 12 or fewer do not move" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 20 TO SC-COUNT
     MOVE 0 TO SC-START
     MOVE 1 TO WS-DIR
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-N1
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-N2
     MOVE -1 TO WS-DIR
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-N3
     MOVE 12 TO SC-COUNT
     MOVE 0 TO SC-START
     MOVE 1 TO WS-DIR
     CALL "STONECUTTER-WHEEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR
     MOVE WS-N1 TO WS-E1
     MOVE WS-N2 TO WS-E2
     MOVE WS-N3 TO WS-E3
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-E4
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "4 8 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-4§4.9 the packet path: Update Recipes (136) through PROTO-PACKET replaces the list; the wheel of the open stonecutter moves the grid by a row" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM PACKET-3
     MOVE PB-LENGTH TO WS-N1
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-PUT-UPDATE-RECIPES" USING PB-BUFFER PB-UPDATE-RECIPES PB-SLOT-DISPLAY-TABLE
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     MOVE 136 TO WS-PACKET
     MOVE 0 TO SC-COUNT
     CALL "PROTO-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN PB-BUFFER WS-PACKET
     MOVE SC-COUNT TO WS-E1
     MOVE 24 TO BM-TYPE
     MOVE 20 TO SC-COUNT
     MOVE 0 TO SC-START
     MOVE -1 TO IN-SCROLL-Y
     CALL "MENU-EXTRA-INPUT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-E2
     MOVE 1 TO IN-SCROLL-Y
     CALL "MENU-EXTRA-INPUT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-E3
     MOVE 0 TO IN-SCROLL-Y
     CALL "MENU-EXTRA-INPUT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SC-START TO WS-E4
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "3 4 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

*> Three entries: stone (10) to a slab (2), stone to stairs (11), stone to bricks (12); written as the server writes them.
 PACKET-3.
     INITIALIZE PB-UPDATE-RECIPES PB-SLOT-DISPLAY-TABLE
     MOVE 0 TO PB-UR-SET-COUNT
     MOVE 3 TO PB-UR-CUT-COUNT
     MOVE 3 TO PB-SDT-COUNT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 3
         MOVE 1 TO PB-UC-INPUT-COUNT(WS-I)
         MOVE 5 TO PB-UC-INPUT(WS-I, 1)
         MOVE WS-I TO PB-UC-DISPLAY(WS-I)
         MOVE PB-SDX-ITEM-STACK TO PB-SDN-TYPE(WS-I)
         COMPUTE PB-SDN-ITEM(WS-I) = 9 + WS-I
         MOVE 1 TO PB-SDN-COUNT(WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 2 TO PB-SDN-COUNT(2)
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-UPDATE-RECIPES" USING PB-BUFFER PB-UPDATE-RECIPES PB-SLOT-DISPLAY-TABLE
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     .

 END PROGRAM TEST-STONECUTTER-SCREEN.

 COPY CLTEST.
